From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-22)
Subject: 0514 sweet_nub: disambiguate withNumber(0) and stop naming OSPtr outside a return type

CI run 44929577157 failed exactly here (full 50 MB log, not a truncated one):

  sweet_nub.cpp:275:25: error: call to 'withNumber' is ambiguous
      OSNumber *maxpower = OSNumber::withNumber(0, 32);
  candidates: withNumber(unsigned long long, unsigned int)
              withNumber(const char *, unsigned int)

`0` is both an integer and a null pointer constant, so both overloads are viable. The fix is
0ULL (and ULL on the other numeric literals, so no future literal can pick the string overload).
The same compile also warned

  sweet_nub.cpp:243:2: warning: use of OSPtr outside of a return type [-Wossharedptr-misuse]

for `OSPtr<OSIterator> children_it = ...`. `auto` keeps the code indifferent to whether OSPtr is
a raw pointer (today) or a shared pointer (if IOKIT_ENABLE_SHARED_PTR is ever enabled), which is
exactly what the header's own comment asks for. OSPtr.h is therefore no longer included.

